{
  "name": "Flexible Casting",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can use your sorcery points to gain additional spell slots, or sacrifice spell slots to gain additional sorcery points. You learn other ways to use your sorcery points as you reach higher levels.</p><p><strong>Creating Spell Slots.</strong> You can transform unexpended sorcery points into one spell slot on your turn (no Action required). The created spell slots vanish at the end of a Long Rest. The Creating Spell Slots table shows the cost of creating a spell slot of a given level. You can create spell slots no higher in level than 5th.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Creating Spell Slots</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Slot Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Sorcery Point Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>7</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Converting a Spell Slot to Sorcery Points.</strong> You can expend one spell slot and gain a number of sorcery points equal to the slot's level (no Action required).</p>",
